From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:21:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 305/306] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Centre the read Vref
 per bit and per byte

The receiver offsets of the data bits (RX_OFFSET_VDQ, one register per
byte for all ranks on Haswell) are set by the sense amplifier training,
from one sample of each value, on the receivers alone, and nothing
looks at them again with data. On a ThinkPad W541 one training in three
of v1.7.0-rc5 left every read margin of channel 1 5 to 9 steps narrower
than the other two, with offsets 1 to 2 codes away.

The read voltage centring of the MRC, after the write voltage, starts
the bits from the middle again and centres each on its own read voltage
margins, then centres the reference of each byte at three read timings
(the trained one and 8 PI ticks to each side), all the ranks of a
channel tested at once. Add HASWELL_NRI_READ_VREF, which does the same.
If the read test fails after it, the training is done again without
the optimisations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I47a97ab642a559669aaeae8ef982d611aa594063
